        "original_id": "f84b669f-282f-57ae-b852-43792bdee351",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Moe Greene, Moe Dalitz, Hyman Martin\n- Works: The Godfather\n- Roles: fictional character, gangster, businessman, casino owner, philanthropist, mobster\n- Places: Pittsburgh\n\nFacts:\n- Moe Dalitz, born Morris Barney Dalitz on December 25, 1899, was an American gangster, businessman, casino owner, and philanthropist.\n- Hyman Martin, also known as \"Pittsburgh Hymie,\" was born on April 6, 1903 and was a Pittsburgh mobster.\n- Moe Greene is a fictional character who appears in Mario Puzo's 1969 novel The Godfather and in the 1972 film adaptation of the same name.\n- Hyman Martin was a close associate of Moe Dalitz and Louis Rothkopf.\n- Moe Dalitz died on August 31, 1989.\n- Hyman Martin died in July 1987.",
